import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.IsFiniteTypeEtaleModuleSheaf

/-!
# Finite values of locally constant etale module sheaves

Source: Stacks Project, Tags 03RU, 03RW(3), and 093N(1); the equivalences are
agent-formulated from these definitions
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-finite-locally-constant-module-values).
-/

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

/-- Over a finite commutative ring, the existence of a trivialization with finite module
values, finite local constancy, and local constancy together with finite type are equivalent.
Every geometric stalk through a member of any such trivialization is isomorphic, as a
module, to that member's constant value.

Proof, following the node:
1. Stalks are module colimits over pointed etale neighbourhoods. The cofiltered-neighbourhood
   lemma and `lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-modules-elementwise` identify their underlying
   abelian groups and show that scalar multiplication acts on germs sectionwise.
2. `lem-weil-pbc-etale-inverse-image-restriction` identifies restriction with inverse image;
   `lem-weil-pbc-inverse-image-stalk-germ` identifies its stalk with the original stalk.
   Naturality for multiplication by each scalar makes this identification module-linear.
3. `lem-weil-pbc-constant-module-sheaf-underlying` and
   `lem-weil-pbc-constant-sheaf-geometric-stalk` identify a constant module sheaf's stalk
   with its value; the constant-presheaf map and germ map are module-linear.
4. Compose these identifications and the stalk of the trivializing isomorphism to obtain
   the moreover assertion (even for values not assumed finite).
5. A finite-value trivialization gives local constancy. Lift any geometric point through
   the etale cover using `lem-weil-pbc-etale-cover-geometric-point-lift`; step 4 gives a
   finite stalk, hence finite local constancy.
6. Conversely, remove empty cover members from a locally constant trivialization. Each
   remaining member has a geometric point, obtained from an algebraic closure of a residue
   field. Step 4 identifies its constant value with a finite stalk, so that value is finite.
7. Finite module values are finitely generated. Apply
   `lem-weil-pbc-locally-constant-finite-values-finite-type` (Stacks 093N(1)) to get finite type.
8. By `lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-module-sheaf-stalk-finitely-generated`, finite type gives
   finitely generated stalks. A stalk generated by `n` elements is a quotient of `Λ^n`,
   hence finite since `Λ` is finite. Together with local constancy this gives (2).

The existing finite-sheaf predicate uses finitely generated stalks at separably closed
points; over a finite ring this is equivalent to finite stalks. Testing at algebraically
closed points is equivalent by invariance under algebraic closure of the geometric field.
Source: Stacks Project, Tags 03RU, 03RW(3), 093N(1), and the stalk calculations of 03PN
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-finite-locally-constant-module-values). -/
theorem finite_locally_constant_module_values_iff
    {Y : Scheme.{u}} {Λ : Type (u + 1)} [CommRing Λ] [Finite Λ]
    (F : Sheaf Y.smallEtaleTopology (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ)) :
    let finiteValues : Prop := ∃ d : LocallyConstantDatum F, ∀ i : d.cover.I₀,
      ∃ M : ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ, Finite M ∧
        Nonempty (F.over (d.cover.etalePrecoverageToEtale i) ≅
          (constantSheaf (Y.smallEtaleTopology.over (d.cover.etalePrecoverageToEtale i))
            (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ)).obj M)
    (finiteValues ↔ IsFiniteLocallyConstantSheaf F) ∧
      (finiteValues ↔ IsLocallyConstantSheaf F ∧ IsFiniteTypeEtaleModuleSheaf F) ∧
      ∀ (d : LocallyConstantDatum F) (M : d.cover.I₀ → ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ),
        (∀ i : d.cover.I₀, Finite (M i) ∧
          Nonempty (F.over (d.cover.etalePrecoverageToEtale i) ≅
            (constantSheaf (Y.smallEtaleTopology.over (d.cover.etalePrecoverageToEtale i))
              (ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ)).obj (M i))) →
        ∀ (i : d.cover.I₀) (Ω : Type u) [Field Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω]
          (s : Spec (.of Ω) ⟶ d.cover.X i),
          Nonempty (((pointSmallEtale (s ≫ d.cover.f i)).sheafFiber
            (A := ModuleCat.{u + 1} Λ)).obj F ≅ M i) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
